description:
FILED s543b (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-16) while fixing #4795.  PRE-EXISTING (base c5f618f2 = the same).  LOUD: PCL dies where perl prints (non-strict code only -- under strict perl refuses the bareword at compile time).

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 | PCL):
    no strict;
    package Bar; sub QQ { "barsub" } sub low { "barlow" }
    package main;
    my $v = QQ; my $w = low; print "$v $w\n";
    # perl: QQ low      PCL: dies "Undefined subroutine &main::QQ called"
EMISSION: `(p-scalar-ctx (pl-QQ))` / `(pl-low)` in package main.

CAUSE: PExpr::_bareword_callable_here's declared-subs scan is PACKAGE-BLIND for an unqualified call site: a `sub QQ` of ANOTHER package declared ABOVE answers 'yes' (callable), so the bare word becomes a call that resolves in the CURRENT package, where nothing is defined.  perl resolves an unqualified name in the current package (or through an import into it), never in a sibling package.  s543b (#4795) made the scan package-aware ONLY when the current package records the name itself (its own constant / sub / import), which is the silent-wrong half; this is the other half.

DIRECTION: skip another package's declaration for an unqualified site always; then a non-ALL-CAPS name answers 'no' (the string, perl's answer); an ALL-CAPS one still meets `_all_caps_guess_here` (a call) and needs the same thought.  This widens the classifier for every multi-package file: gate-SET scan over both populations + the full sweep, as #4795.
